window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>He’s hiding a dark secret, one that will change my life forever.</p> <p>I shouldn’t be here.</p> <p>Forced to move school partway through my senior year.</p> <p>The Syndicate Academy is the embodiment of everything I hate.</p> <p>An academy for heirs of tyrants like my parents.</p> <p>I hate it here, except for one part, Principal Oakley Byrne.</p> <p>The most gorgeous man I’ve ever met, with piercing aquamarine eyes.</p> <p>He’s dark, brooding, and not your average Principal.</p> <p>I’m drawn to him by a magnetic force, but I repel him.</p> <p>Despite his cold treatment, I can’t help but tempt the beast to come out to play.</p> <p>An action I’ll soon regret.</p> <p>This man hides dark secrets behind his walls.</p> <p>Secrets that could destroy my family and me.</p> <p>They say all is fair in love and war.</p> <p>I can’t be a part of a war I never knew existed.</p> <p>He intends to devour me whole and spit me out, leaving my world in tatters.</p> <p>The question is, will I survive his wrath?</p> <p>Sinister Games is the first book in the Syndicate Academy Series. This book can be listened to as a standalone and has a happily ever after ending. This story has dark themes, hot scenes, violence, content some listeners may find upsetting, and bad language.</p> <p>*Originally titled Corrupt Educator</p>"; 
